# IFileAttacher and FileAttacher

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Contracts`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Components.Core`

Kernel-locked contracts for the component used to attach files to chat messages.

```csharp
public interface IFileAttacher : IComponent
{
    EventCallback<KernelContent[]> OnItemsAdded { get; set; }
}

public abstract class FileAttacher : KernelComponentBase, IFileAttacher
{
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<KernelContent[]> OnItemsAdded { get; set; }
}
```

## Purpose
The chat UI renders whatever `IFileAttacher` implementation is currently selected to let the user attach files (drag-and-drop, paste, file picker, etc.). When the user finalises a selection, the component fires `OnItemsAdded` with the resolved `KernelContent` items, which the parent chat message service persists.

## Members

### `IFileAttacher.OnItemsAdded`
- `EventCallback<KernelContent[]>` — fired when the user has added one or more content items to the current message.
- The interface inherits from `IComponent` because the attacher is itself a renderable Blazor component.

### `FileAttacher` (abstract base class)
- Inherits from `KernelComponentBase`, so it has access to the active `Kernel` and can use `[KernelInject]`.
- Provides `OnItemsAdded` as a default `[Parameter]` so derived classes just override the render output.
- Concrete implementations register via `InterfaceOverrides.UseFileAttacher<T>()`.

## Selection Mechanism
The runtime picks a concrete `IFileAttacher` from `InterfaceOverrides.FileAttacher` (which defaults to `null`/built-in). To override:

```csharp
public class MyAssistantMode : IAssistantMode
{
    public async Task ConfigureAsync(CyrenaKernelBuilder builder)
    {
        var overrides = builder.GetFeatureOption<InterfaceOverrides>();
        overrides.UseFileAttacher<MyCustomAttacher>();
    }
}
```

## Related
- `KernelComponentBase` — base class for the abstract `FileAttacher`
- `InterfaceOverrides.UseFileAttacher<T>()` — selects which `IFileAttacher` is active
- `IFileHandlerFactory` — produces the `KernelContent` items that get fired through `OnItemsAdded`
